"""Focused four-page report for the arithmetic experiment, built from recorded evidence."""
from pathlib import Path
import json
from reportlab.platypus import SimpleDocTemplate,Paragraph,Table,TableStyle,Spacer,PageBreak,Preformatted
from reportlab.lib.styles import getSampleStyleSheet,ParagraphStyle
from reportlab.lib import colors
from reportlab.lib.pagesizes import A4

root=Path(__file__).resolve().parent; runs=root/'code/runs'; reports=root/'reports'
e=json.loads((runs/'arithmetic-search/experiments-arithmetic.json').read_text()); robust=json.loads((runs/'arithmetic-search/robustness.json').read_text()); ablate=json.loads((runs/'arithmetic-search/ablation.json').read_text()); frozen=json.loads((runs/'freeze-arithmetic.json').read_text()); resources=json.loads((runs/'arithmetic-validation-resources.json').read_text()); final_score=json.loads((runs/'arithmetic-test-score.json').read_text()); final_resources=json.loads((runs/'arithmetic-test-resources.json').read_text())
styles=getSampleStyleSheet(); styles.add(ParagraphStyle(name='ABody',fontName='Helvetica',fontSize=10,leading=14,spaceAfter=9,textColor=colors.HexColor('#243345')));styles.add(ParagraphStyle(name='AHead',fontName='Helvetica-Bold',fontSize=19,leading=23,spaceAfter=14,textColor=colors.HexColor('#123149')));styles.add(ParagraphStyle(name='ASub',fontName='Helvetica-Bold',fontSize=11,leading=15,spaceBefore=5,spaceAfter=6,textColor=colors.HexColor('#087E8B')));styles.add(ParagraphStyle(name='ASmall',parent=styles['ABody'],fontSize=8.5,leading=11));styles.add(ParagraphStyle(name='ACode',fontName='Courier',fontSize=8,leading=11,spaceAfter=9))
story=[];md=[]
def p(t,style='ABody'):story.append(Paragraph(t,styles[style]));md.append(t)
def page(title):
    if story:story.append(PageBreak());md.append('\n---\n')
    p(title,'AHead')
def table(headers,rows,widths):
    data=[[Paragraph(str(x),styles['ASmall']) for x in row] for row in [headers]+rows];t=Table(data,colWidths=widths,repeatRows=1)
    t.setStyle(TableStyle([('BACKGROUND',(0,0),(-1,0),colors.HexColor('#E7F1F4')),('ROWBACKGROUNDS',(0,1),(-1,-1),[colors.white,colors.HexColor('#F5F7FA')]),('VALIGN',(0,0),(-1,-1),'TOP'),('TOPPADDING',(0,0),(-1,-1),5),('BOTTOMPADDING',(0,0),(-1,-1),5),('LEFTPADDING',(0,0),(-1,-1),7)]));story.extend([t,Spacer(1,10)]);md.append(str([headers]+rows))
def code(t):story.append(Preformatted(t,styles['ACode']));md.append('```\n'+t+'\n```')

page('Selecting Reliable LLM Reasoning:\nArithmetic Evidence')
p('DASE7506 MP2 | Follow-up experiment | 31 October 2026','ASmall')
p('This experiment asks whether inexpensive, mechanically checkable arithmetic evidence improves candidate selection beyond the supplied representations and trace statistics. It adds eighteen deterministic features describing numerical equation consistency, then chooses a compact linear ranker using training-only question-level cross-validation. No new language-model generation, external dataset or pretrained weights are used.')
table(['Evaluation','Original submitted verifier','Frozen arithmetic verifier'],[['Training OOF, seed 2026','90.81% (4318/4755)','91.65% (4358/4755)'],['Reshuffled train OOF, seed 2037','90.75%','91.84%'],['Validation','92.23% (736/798)','94.24% (752/798)'],['Official public test score','81.37% (380/467)','82.44% (385/467)']],[195,150,150])
p('<b>The frozen verifier scores 385/467 = 82.44111349% on the official public test bank.</b> This is five more correct choices than the original submitted model (+1.07 percentage points). One final scoring run is performed after explicit authorization and source/asset hash verification. No model parameters, features or settings are changed after that score; the original score record is preserved.')
p('Task, data and protocol','ASub')
p('Each question has four supplied candidate solutions. Select one candidate index; the unchanged official scorer checks its final numeric answer, not the validity of every reasoning step. The bank has 4,755 training, 798 validation and 467 test questions. All groups contain a correct final answer, and several candidates can be correct. Only training references fit parameters and normalization. Validation is inspected after the current configuration is selected. Test inputs/references are not opened during development; the later final evaluation only scores the fixed checkpoint.')
p('The original baseline is the training-standardized C=0.01 logistic verifier over embeddings, centered embeddings and 46 statistics. Earlier frozen public-test scores are 81.37% for the original model and 80.09% for the CPU ranking follow-up; the GPU round is not test-scored. All records are retained. The test bank was observed in earlier project rounds, so the current result is not a pristine independent generalization study. An instructor audit remains necessary for stronger conclusions.')
p('Main evidence','ASub')
p('The selected ranker gains forty training-OOF questions over the original verifier, with the direction retained under a reshuffled partition. A matched loss/regularization ablation gains twenty questions when arithmetic features are added. The parser checks at least one numeric equality in 63.57% of training candidate traces, but it deliberately skips many unsupported expressions. Arithmetic consistency is informative without being a proof of correct interpretation.')

page('1. Bounded arithmetic checks and ranker')
p('Conservative numeric extraction','ASub')
p('The checker normalizes supported LaTex fractions, multiplication/division signs, parentheses, percentages and grouped thousands. It examines adjacent sides of equality signs only when numeric expressions can be extracted. A bounded AST interpreter accepts numeric constants and arithmetic operators; it does not execute Python eval, calls, names, indexing or attributes. Expression length, recursion depth, exponent size and fraction bit length are capped. Division by zero and unsupported syntax are rejected.')
p('Checks cover fractions, decimals, signs, powers and percentages. A comparison is accepted within 1% relative tolerance plus 1e-6; a literal decimal right side additionally allows half a unit of its displayed precision. This accommodates common rounded answers. Unit annotations and unknown algebraic expressions can cause the equality to be skipped. The feature extractor is a heuristic span parser, so lack of a flag is not evidence that a trace is correct.')
table(['Feature group','Examples'],[['Counts and coverage','Checked, inconsistent and consistent equations; raw equalities; supported coverage'],['Severity and final-answer relation','Inconsistency fraction; maximum/mean relative discrepancy; last check; checks sharing the final numeric answer'],['Structure and agreement','Division and exact-equality fractions; relative inconsistency versus peers; mean inconsistency for candidates sharing an answer']],[175,320])
p('Eighteen arithmetic features are appended to the original 1,024-dimensional embedding and 46 statistics, giving 1,088 input dimensions. No arithmetic result is used as a hard veto: a trace with a bad step can still have a correct final answer, and parsing can be incomplete. Training determines how much predictive weight these features receive.')
p('Objective and inference','ASub')
p('The selected model uses marginal listwise loss. For each informative training group, it minimizes logsumexp over valid candidate scores minus logsumexp over correct candidate scores, plus 0.1 times squared weight norm divided by two. Groups with no valid wrong candidate contribute no selection information after masking and are excluded from this fitting loss. StandardScaler uses training candidates only; L-BFGS-B fits a single linear weight vector with zero intercept. Prediction chooses the largest score among candidates that the official parser can read.')
code('x_ij = [embedding_ij, original_statistics_ij, arithmetic_ij]\nz_ij = w^T ((x_ij - training_mean) / training_scale)\nloss_i = logsumexp(valid z_i) - logsumexp(correct z_i)\nchoice_i = argmax_j z_ij     (invalid parsed answers masked)')
p('The numeric checker does not understand the question, units or physical meaning. For example, 94 - 46 = 48 is arithmetically true even if 46 counts pairs while 94 counts people. It can only provide partial evidence for the full selection task.','ASmall')

page('2. Comparisons, ablation and uncertainty')
p('The recorded search compares the original baseline and nine arithmetic candidates: three pointwise BCE regularization settings, three pairwise logistic settings and three marginal-listwise settings. All model selection uses three question-disjoint training folds with seed 2026. The original baseline wins ties. A preliminary parser-debug run is aborted before validation; partial-expression rejection tests are added and the corrected search is run in full. The partial debug log is retained separately.')
rows=[]
for c in e['candidates']:rows.append([c['name'],f"{100*c['oof_accuracy']:.2f}"])
table(['Training-OOF configuration','Accuracy %'],rows,[382,113])
p('The arithmetic winner is marginal_combined_0.1. It fixes 166 original OOF errors and introduces 126, for a net gain of forty. A paired question bootstrap with 5,000 resamples and seed 2026 gives a descriptive gain interval of +0.15 to +1.54 percentage points. The interval does not correct for selecting among configurations, overlapping fold-training data or adaptation across earlier project rounds.')
table(['Diagnostic (same training bank)','Control','Selected candidate'],[['Matched objective/regularization; omit arithmetic','91.23% (4338/4755)','91.65% (4358/4755)'],['Reshuffled three-fold diagnostic, seed 2037','90.75% original verifier','91.84% arithmetic ranker']],[245,125,125])
p('The matched feature ablation holds the loss, regularization, numeric parser and folds constant; adding arithmetic features gains twenty questions (+0.42 points). The complete method versus the original verifier also changes its training objective, so the full +0.84-point gain cannot be attributed only to arithmetic features. The reshuffled diagnostic evaluates the already selected method and does not trigger another configuration search. It reuses the same questions, so it is not an external audit.')
p('Only after training-OOF selection and full training is the selected configuration evaluated on validation: 752/798 = 94.23558897%. A later, separately authorized final evaluation of this same frozen model gives 385/467 = 82.44111349%. The improvement is modest and descriptive of the course bank; no statistical significance or generalization guarantee is claimed. The recorded freeze, original development-only plan and subsequent final-scoring authorization remain separate provenance records.','ASmall')

page('3. Limits, resources and reproduction')
p('What arithmetic evidence misses','ASub')
p('In training, at least one inconsistency is flagged in 1.63% of candidates with a correct final answer and 6.02% of candidates with a wrong final answer. The association is useful but imperfect: erroneous intermediate steps can cancel, a final answer can be correct by chance, and extraction or rounding heuristics can be incomplete. These rates describe candidate-level final-answer labels, not human-verified step correctness.')
p('Post-selection validation diagnostics illustrate the limits. For the stock-profit question at position 48, the original verifier selects 100 and the new pipeline selects the reference answer 40; this change cannot be causally attributed to the arithmetic features alone. At position 52, the dog/rabbit question should yield four minutes, but both methods still select eight. The relevant unit-bearing equations are skipped by the conservative parser. At position 44, both still select 48 for the pairing problem, because its arithmetic is valid despite counting the wrong quantity. The ambiguous paperclip reference at position 32 also remains unresolved.')
p('Resources and integrity checks','ASub')
p(f"All fitting uses CPU with four numerical-library threads. The corrected search takes {e['total_seconds']:.2f} s locally; reshuffled diagnostic {robust['seconds']:.2f} s and matched ablation {ablate['seconds']:.2f} s. Partial debug timing is retained separately. Required inference assets total {frozen['inference_asset_bytes']:,} bytes. Fresh official CPU prediction plus scoring takes {resources['total_wall_seconds']:.3f} s on validation and {final_resources['total_wall_seconds']:.3f} s on the complete test bank, on an Intel Core i7-13650HX. These include startup/imports, hashing, loading and preprocessing. The reference Xeon is not measured.")
p('Behavioral numeric/LaTex/rounding/unit/unsafe-expression checks pass. Float32 export preserves every validation choice. Renamed IDs, a seven-question bank and candidate score permutations pass. The official data, numeric parser and scorer remain unchanged. Inference receives new bank/array inputs and never opens references, stored predictions or answer lookup tables. Frozen source/asset hashes are recorded in runs/freeze-arithmetic.json.')
p('Exact commands from code/','ASub')
code('python -m pip install -r requirements.txt\npython download_data.py\npython check_arithmetic.py\npython evaluate_arithmetic.py           # validation\npython evaluate_arithmetic_final.py     # official test reproduction\n\n# Optional training and diagnostics (no test IO)\npython -m pip install -r requirements-training.txt\npython train_arithmetic.py\npython check_robustness_arithmetic.py\npython ablate_arithmetic.py')
p('The inference assets are runs/model_bundle_arithmetic. Training-only selection and full records are in train_arithmetic.py and runs/arithmetic-search/. Dependencies remain NumPy 1.26.4, SciPy 1.13.1, scikit-learn 1.5.1, joblib 1.4.2 and threadpoolctl 3.5.0. Seeds are recorded in the plan and diagnostics. Checkpoint evaluation requires NumPy only.','ASmall')
p('AI/reuse disclosure: Codex substantially assisted with design, implementation, debugging, experiments, analysis and report writing. Official course tools are reused unchanged. Questions/references derive from GSM8K (retained MIT license); candidates/embeddings derive from Qwen3-0.6B with revision in the manifest. No additional data or pretrained weights are used. Course source: github.com/xudongwu-0/DASE7506-MP2, upstream bb801f4f2e7629d270df765ab12c333b2dc616bb. The matching frozen source/checkpoint and official JSON are published together for reproduction.','ASmall')

